<title>USA: USDA to raise some dairy grading, inspection fees.</title>
<headline>USDA to raise some dairy grading, inspection fees.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it will raise certain fees for industry-solicited grading and inspection services funded by the dairy industry, effective January 5.</p>
<p>The new rates are from $48 per hour to $52 per hour for intermittent grading and inspection services, with additional travel and per diem costs continuing to be charged, and from $43 per hour to $47 per hour for continuous resident grading and inspection by a grader-inspector permanently assigned to a plant.</p>
<p>USDA said the rates reflect increased operating costs.</p>
</text>
